==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 10.67~18.67 seconds<sup>320f~560f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 20~53.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~53.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Hippoe]] spawns as the boss.
**6 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.

==Strategy==
These enemies are no joke, despite what it may look like. Each is insanely buffed, to the point where they can instantly kill nearly anything, and even the strongest [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless Cats]] will need multiple attacks to eliminate them. Luckily, all enemies keep their awfully short ranges and Hippoe is the only one with Area Attack.

Bring generalist [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] of your own, and make sure to kill the peons first so your meatshields can stall the boss. It will help a lot to mostly use cheap meatshields if you can, but still use [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] for its speed and health. Money is quite tight here, as the peons don't drop a lot of cash while taking extremely long to kill.

Non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] units that work especially well in this stage include, but are not limited to: [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]], [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]], [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]], [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

